     {
      "_key": "7d3c3e51",
      "cls": "elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-heading",
      "_type": "heading",
      "tag": "p",
      "html": "Frequently Asked Questions About <span style=\"color:#366797\">Teeth Whitening</span>"
     },
     {
      "_key": "1c7c7d31",
      "cls": "elementor-widget-n-accordion",
      "_type": "accordion",
      "items": [
       {
        "_key": "42c53c6f",
        "title": "How long do teeth whitening results last?",
        "open": true,
        "content": {
         "_type": "box",
         "_key": "42c53c6f",
         "cls": "e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child",
         "children": [
          {
           "_key": "1b3e1574",
           "cls": "elementor-widget-text-editor",
           "_type": "text",
           "html": "<p>Results can last anywhere from 6 months to 2 years depending on your oral hygiene, diet, and lifestyle habits. Avoiding coffee, red wine, and tobacco can help extend your results.</p>"
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "_key": "4851e60d",
        "title": "Will my teeth be sensitive afterward?",
        "open": false,
        "content": {
         "_type": "box",
         "_key": "4851e60d",
         "cls": "e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child",
         "children": [
          {
           "_key": "2c9219aa",
           "cls": "elementor-widget-text-editor",
           "_type": "text",
           "html": "<p>Some patients experience mild sensitivity, but our treatments are designed to minimize discomfort. We’ll also recommend aftercare tips and products to help reduce any sensitivity.</p>"
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "_key": "3ea233b2",
        "title": "Is professional whitening better than over-the-counter options?",
        "open": false,
        "content": {
         "_type": "box",
         "_key": "3ea233b2",
         "cls": "e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child",
         "children": [
          {
           "_key": "3bc8dca8",
           "cls": "elementor-widget-text-editor",
           "_type": "text",
           "html": "<p>Yes. Professional treatments use stronger, dentist-supervised formulas that remove deeper stains and deliver faster, longer-lasting results without damaging enamel.</p>"
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "_key": "246a6674",
        "title": "Is teeth whitening safe?",
        "open": false,
        "content": {
         "_type": "box",
         "_key": "246a6674",
         "cls": "e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child",
         "children": [
          {
           "_key": "6981d34c",
           "cls": "elementor-widget-text-editor",
           "_type": "text",
           "html": "<p>When performed under dental supervision, whitening is completely safe for your teeth and gums. Learn more about safety recommendations from the Cleveland Clinic.</p>"
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "_key": "1c552253",
        "title": "How white will my teeth get?",
        "open": false,
        "content": {
         "_type": "box",
         "_key": "1c552253",
         "cls": "e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child",
         "children": [
          {
           "_key": "43021cd9",
           "cls": "elementor-widget-text-editor",
           "_type": "text",
           "html": "<p>Whitening results vary by individual, but most patients see a 2–8 shade improvement. We’ll give you a realistic expectation based on your current tooth color and type of staining.</p>"
          }
         ]
        }
       }
      ],
